ttachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T19:23:04-07:00","id":1388531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1387666-wanna-play-an-elemetal-hero-go-solar-~\ud83d\udc96?p=1388505#post1388505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't Falling Tears Poet also really independent?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, he had apartments provided and furnished courtesy of his Liege and a huge hammer, at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T21:19:28-07:00","id":1388554,"title":"","content":"And the Raiton NPC also serves the Neverborn (or so they claim) so it may not even be a free-floating exaltation, which make it's even worse. Since even with free-floating exaltation you still got butt-blasted by a bunch of powerful Elders.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T22:12:47-07:00","id":1388568,"title":"","content":"By that rubric, the Neverborn <i>existing at all</i> would stand inherently in the way of your concept of a free Abyssal.<br /> <br /> Remember, the Neverborn do not possess agency or even coherent motivations - they just want to die.<br /> <br /> Raiton\u2019s claim to serve them could very well be (and likely is) entirely metaphorical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T23:06:56-07:00","id":1388578,"title":"","content":"Raiton was written up in 2nd edition where the Neverborn did possess agency. For example, when the First and Forsaken Lion screwed up during the Great Contagion, one of the Neverborn summoned him to its tomb where it punished him for his actions by trapping him in his armor. Something similar happen to Princess Magnificent where the Neverborn directly punished her and made her serve the First and Forsaken Lion because of her failings. It's very likely that the Neverborn will operate differently in 3rd edition, but at least in 2nd edition they had at least some agency, enough to be able to personally and directly punish the Deathlords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T23:55:38-07:00","id":1388857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1387666-wanna-play-an-elemetal-hero-go-solar-~\ud83d\udc96?p=1387670#post1387670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigent seems better, imo, if you're absolutely set on a lightning themed brawler. Exigent of Storms or Thunder, maybe.<br /> <br /> Solars are top end, obviously, but they're still got a color theme going on of golden sunlight. Not something to fit lightning, you see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor color alterations are easily done via either custom control spells or custom evocations.<br /> <br /> &quot;The color of your anima, along with any of your native charms that share its color scheme, becomes tinted with blue as it crackles with phantom electricity.&quot; This seems like a fairly reasonable part of the control spell effect for a lightning spell.<br /> <br /> I mean... it's not like you really <i>need</i> a reason for something that's just cosmetic, but that's there if you want it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T00:38:25-07:00","id":1388859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1387666-wanna-play-an-elemetal-hero-go-solar-~\ud83d\udc96?p=1388578#post1388578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very likely that the Neverborn will operate differently in 3rd edition\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not just \u201clikely.\u201d We\u2019ve been <i>told</i>, every time we ask, that the Abyssal/Deathlord/Neverborn setup <b>will be different.</b> <br /> <br /> \u2022The Abyssals will not be the slaves of the Deathlords. <br /> \u2022The Deathlords will not be thirteen-but-really-nine-because-we-didn\u2019t-write-a-setting-that-<i>really</i>-has-room-for-thirteen-so-yeah-nine omnipotent tyrants who don\u2019t <i>really</i> need Abyssals if they ever decide to get serious and destroy the world, and only keep them around because it amuses them.<br /> \u2022The Neverborn will not be all-seeing hair-trigger-temper grandmas who disapprove of everything you are and do, and whose ass-whupping hand has an infinite reach.<br /> <br /> Expecting them to go back on their word <i>now</i> is pretty irrational, wouldn\u2019t you say?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-16-2020, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T04:33:30-07:00","id":1388878,"title":"","content":"The setup for Weeping Raiton in MoEP: Abyssals originally left it open that she might be some grifter, but Scroll of Exalts abandoned it in favour of using those characteristics for Merticulous Owl retconned into a Moonshadow thus they ended up portraying her with Immortal Malevolence Enslavement.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T06:02:11-07:00","id":1388902,"title":"","content":"Isn\u2019t that the book that reveals that the iconic dusk caste hates the iconic midnight caste, all just for being prettier than her?<br /> <br /> I have some issues with that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T06:52:24-07:00","id":1388919,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's a lot that could be done in 3e, IMO for the better, to make Deathlords more ghost-like and less like an Exalt in a ghost mask. Abyssals have tended to have a thing where it's like being Skeletor's or Exdeath's Henchmen, where you sort of hang around his evil spooky castle and do his dark bidding (not on the internet). Which is kind of like because I think they wanted to emphasize these ideas of &quot;You've sold away your soul for powerful servitude&quot; and &quot;Apprentice of the Sith&quot; things as part of the Abyssals game. <br /> <br /> But actually I think as a setting Exalted may be better served by placing the Deathlords more as powerful and scary, very inhuman, chaotic, tortured, malevolent fragments-of-a-person that can incarnate only partially and in specific places and circumstances, and less like an Exalt that's free to move around the setting as they please, and then placing Abyssals as their vassals who rule distant kingdoms in their name or outriders sent on distant quests. Avoids the sort of problems of having powerful NPCs around with that much free agency, while still leaving them as present as a challenging conflict, should you arrange circumstances to confront them.<br /> <br /> (There's a lot that can be done with Abyssals and Deathlords generally. I'd love to see them broaden away from Abyssals as &quot;goth-clown-psycho-killer&quot; and &quot;Yoshitako Amano undead bishounen knight&quot;, with a side order of &quot;corrupt taoist immortal&quot; to some wider imagery that still leans on feudal societies. This is something more people have done in games and talked about, I feel like the core setting hasn't so much.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T12:39:18-07:00","id":1389038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1387666-wanna-play-an-elemetal-hero-go-solar-~\ud83d\udc96?p=1388859#post1388859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not just \u201clikely.\u201d We\u2019ve been <i>told</i>, every time we ask, that the Abyssal/Deathlord/Neverborn setup <b>will be different.</b><br /> <br /> \u2022The Abyssals will not be the slaves of the Deathlords.<br /> \u2022The Deathlords will not be thirteen-but-really-nine-because-we-didn\u2019t-write-a-setting-that-<i>really</i>-has-room-for-thirteen-so-yeah-nine omnipotent tyrants who don\u2019t <i>really</i> need Abyssals if they ever decide to get serious and destroy the world, and only keep them around because it amuses them.<br /> \u2022The Neverborn will not be all-seeing hair-trigger-temper grandmas who disapprove of everything you are and do, and whose ass-whupping hand has an infinite reach.<br /> <br /> Expecting them to go back on their word <i>now</i> is pretty irrational, wouldn\u2019t you say?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if you took umbrage to that. I was talking about 2nd edition where the Neverborn absolutely had agency. We haven't seen the Neverborn get written up in 3rd edition yet.<br /> <br /> Now, I don't believe that the Dev's are going to backtrack - though to note, there is a difference between the Neverborn being omniscient smiting ur-monsters and having some level of agency. For example, is it possible that they can hand out some sort of punishment to Deathlords who fail or rebel? I don't know that the developers have said that the Neverborn are totally <i>incapable</i> of punishing wayward or rebellious servants in some way. <br /> <br /> Regardless, when it comes to talking about what may or may not be in the books in the future (regardless what RPG or what developers are being discussed, or even if it's a different genre like a novel or video game or movie) when I talk about material developers have said they want to include or plan to include, I always approach it with the attitude of, &quot;This is very likely what we'll see,&quot; rather than, &quot;This is absolutely what we'll see,&quot; because as a very wise puppet once said, &quot;Always in motion is the future.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's just a personal quirk of mine when it comes to discussing future stuff that has yet to be printed. Sorry if that set you off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-16-2020, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T16:42:04-07:00","id":1389115,"title":"","content":"Nah, it's cool. Just, fate/God/the universe would have to absolutely <i>hate us</i> in order to put us in the timeline that gives us both COVID-19 <i>and </i>a rehash of everything that made 2e Abyssals awful in 3e. A cold, uncaring universe wouldn't do that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T15:43:39-07:00","id":1390637,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, which Manhua does &quot;Purple Mad Lightning&quot; come from, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar298_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"298\" data-vbnamecard=\"298\">Jen</a>? Judging by your illustration, he looks, in the best possible meaning of the word, &quot;Sick&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12641-aldosalt","name":"AldoSalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12641_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T22:54:24-07:00","id":1390710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AldoSalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1387666-wanna-play-an-elemetal-hero-go-solar-~\ud83d\udc96?p=1390637#post1390637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, which Manhua does &quot;Purple Mad Lightning&quot; come from, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar298_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"298\" data-vbnamecard=\"298\">Jen</a>? Judging by your illustration, he looks, in the best possible meaning of the word, &quot;Sick&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>He's from Clashing War of Mountain and Sea (\u5c71\u6d77\u9006\u6218) by Khoo Fuk Lung, though he's just a side character sadly TT.TT<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}